A||||11||Klown||Instrument Panel Bulbs||||5||
Z||000000||Klown||04-23-2001||05:59 PM||||One of the lights in my instrument panel just went so I opened up the back of the panel to see what I would have to replace.  The bulbs are a screw in type but they don't have any markings.  Does anyone know what the wattage is for these bulbs or if they have a replacement code I should look for when I go the auto parts store to replace them?  One more thing, I noticed I had a total of 14 bulbs but there were spots for 2 or 3 more.  Am I missing any or are these just not used on the Fiero?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-23-2001||06:02 PM||||I believe they are all # 194.<P>They are push-in bulbs that mount into the quarter turn screw in holders.<P>You can get them at Walmart or just about any other store that carries auto bulbs.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||shiloh187||04-23-2001||06:28 PM||||i just took my dash out and noticed there were spots for 3 more on mine also, so i assume it is normal..<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierofreek2001||04-23-2001||11:29 PM||||is there any bulbs out there that will fit in the dash that are brighter?  the ones i have just arent cutting it...<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||Thor||04-23-2001||11:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierofreek2001:<BR><B>is there any bulbs out there that will fit in the dash that are brighter?  the ones i have just arent cutting it...<BR>steve</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>...Just a thought...Have you tried adjusting the instrument light reastat/dial, located just under the headlight switch?...If you have and there has been no change in brightness then the culprit may be with the reastat. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||04-24-2001||01:57 AM||||could be dusty and dirty in side. You could try taking it apart and cleaning it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierofreek2001||04-24-2001||10:18 AM||||..... um yeah i have tried the dimmer switch, its all the way up<P>so i guess brighter bulbs isnt the answer huh?   because i know that taking that whole assembly apart to clean takes hours and hours...<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||04-24-2001||04:39 PM||||Watch out on brighter bulbs.  More heat could damage the dash.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Taijiguy||04-24-2001||04:58 PM||||They make those 194's in a halogen now. But they are pricey, especially if you are going to replace 6 or 8 of them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||07:38 PM||||some are always unused. like the shift lite in an automatic car. some dont have overheat lite either. I wouldnt put in a briter bulb for the heat reason too. its gets pretty hot inside the dash, could cause some wiring to melt. I put in Ferrari lighted switches in mine for head and parking lites and drilled a series of holes beside them for cooling (you cant see them).<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||04-24-2001||07:45 PM||||Rodney has some brighter ones made specifically for the dash. Here's his site: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||04-24-2001||09:43 PM||||Hey Klown!<BR>When you replace those lamps, be sure to clean the printed circuit with a pencil eraser...<BR>Sometimes they will go intermittant if you don't clean em first...<BR>If you do open up the instrument cluster to clean it, spray with bright aluminum paint to increase the reflectivity...<BR>crash... ||||reg||1
